{"title":"2013 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine all polynomials <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> with real coefficients such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/f/4cf66fa442582c1f655233cf0d89bcc1c81c3fb7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x+1)P(x-1)-(x-1)P(x)\\]\" width=\"239\" height=\"18\" />\nis a constant polynomial.     \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93bfaa38a09dbb96291bf936fbbaa47c101e4072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x)=(x+1)P(x-1)-(x-1)P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"308\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/a/64a6c32f179c2f06678dac0d272e60fc3d833539.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)=\\sum_{i=0}^{n}c_ix^i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"123\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/f/b7f18eed39d0fde81593511f7be13e0977b09ecb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x)=(x+1)\\sum_{i=0}^{n}(x-1)^ic_i-(x-1)\\sum_{i=0}^{n}c_ix^i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"363\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b92ddd2ec9575bfab9cc9d270c3bf1fd4befd9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x)=\\sum_{i=0}^{n}x(x-1)^ic_i+\\sum_{i=0}^{n}(x-1)^ic_i-\\sum_{i=0}^{n}c_ix^{i+1}+\\sum_{i=0}^{n}c_ix^i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"479\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/6/0f67c43c3aefd99d0647f4f16774c4b60bb7dcc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=0}^{n}(x-1)^ic_i=\\sum_{j=0}^{n}\\left( \\sum_{i=j}^{n}(-1)^{i-j}\\binom{i}{i-j}c_i \\right)x^j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"367\" height=\"58\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/1696a63951dc4dc9d635be9ceb62275d9cdefeed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=0}^{n}x(x-1)^ic_i=\\sum_{j=0}^{n}\\left( \\sum_{i=j}^{n}(-1)^{i-j}\\binom{i}{i-j}c_i \\right)x^{j+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"398\" height=\"58\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/0/a1073ffe111a8164c7f5d872f7c1596710399d97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x)=\\sum_{j=0}^{n}\\left( \\sum_{i=j}^{n}(-1)^{i-j}\\binom{i}{i-j}c_i \\right)x^j+\\sum_{j=0}^{n}\\left( \\sum_{i=j}^{n}(-1)^{i-j}\\binom{i}{i-j}c_i \\right)x^{j+1}-\\sum_{i=0}^{n}c_ix^{i+1}+\\sum_{i=0}^{n}c_ix^i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"763\" height=\"58\" />\n</p><p>In order for the new polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de8fdaa56ea5a8940d4bba79faa9e3dea0f6bf7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> to be a constant, all the coefficients in front of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c65a6467332273f4d68d2b564d2019cf94b42104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^i$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/3/b934ca27da25038445a99a7898871ee70d0d9ac6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> need to be zero.\n</p><p>So we start by looking at the coefficient in front of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/91901196e5eb6f0de651a686782e6d4fd3c19bea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( c_2-c_1+\\sum_{i=2}^{n}(-1)^{i-2}\\binom{i}{i-2}c_i+\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(-1)^{i-1}\\binom{i}{i-1}c_i \\right)x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"477\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8755e807cc74887a7841263e39f992f47d7b90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(-1)^{i-1}\\binom{i}{i-1}c_i=c_1+\\sum_{i=2}^{n}(-1)^{i-1}\\binom{i}{i-1}c_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"393\" height=\"55\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/a/24a0ebff67336b7dc4fa496784008d1b778d32b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( c_2-c_1+c_1+\\sum_{i=2}^{n}(-1)^{i-2}\\binom{i}{i-2}c_i+\\sum_{i=2}^{n}(-1)^{i-1}\\binom{i}{i-1}c_i \\right)x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"515\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/5261060549370d49e86a244cb0f2e46326916081.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( c_2+\\sum_{i=2}^{n}\\left((-1)^{i-2}\\binom{i}{i-2}+(-1)^{i-1}\\binom{i}{i-1} \\right)c_i\\right)x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"435\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>We then evaluate the term of the sum when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f3e5193f4abdbaf8c424028753f296dac345eb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=2$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/0/d70b0018dfdf4cba7b6fac8c2024c48acf283a1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( c_2+(1-2)c_2+\\sum_{i=3}^{n}\\left((-1)^{i-2}\\binom{i}{i-2}+(-1)^{i-1}\\binom{i}{i-1} \\right)c_i\\right)x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"527\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/9/8f9a1384fb27dbfe4c103ccda5f99737d1aa46b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\sum_{i=3}^{n}\\left((-1)^{i-2}\\binom{i}{i-2}+(-1)^{i-1}\\binom{i}{i-1} \\right)c_i\\right)x^2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"431\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Note that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/3/0134af18ca53751c9f9ec73d48b7fa0ff8da9ea6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/00322295674c54c5413520f7493470ff32ae3cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d4142d351ef99cc26a94e44c1912d904dd4a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> are not present in the expression before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, they can be anything and the coefficient in front of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is still zero because the expression before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48524d3889ec8433cb03669176e738011df245b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> also starts with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/a/94aaab012b431d7695fa1ae72d7a88b05baf09f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, and the expression before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f0078b54474db2dbf6219e8386b9b62c4405c94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4$\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> also starts with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67cff48f601f12a5b71afe302e7c3487f7535731.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and so on...\n</p><p>In fact in matrix form when solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e95be43c04d6869c67861aae1e3e69123fedd8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> for for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, it will look something like this:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd219f39799cc35c1fa215c69ae3044d53cba22c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{bmatrix} 2 &amp; -1 &amp; 1 &amp; -1 &amp; 1 &amp; -1 &amp;\\cdots &amp; K_{0n}\\\\ 0 &amp; 1 &amp; -1 &amp; 2 &amp; -3 &amp; 4 &amp;  \\cdots &amp; K_{1n}\\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 2 &amp; -5 &amp; \\cdots &amp; K_{2n}\\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; -1 &amp; 2 &amp; 0 &amp; \\cdots &amp; K_{3n}\\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; -2 &amp; 5 &amp; \\cdots &amp; K_{4n}\\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; -3 &amp; \\cdots &amp; K_{5n}\\\\ \\vdots &amp;\\vdots &amp;\\vdots &amp;\\vdots &amp;\\vdots &amp;\\vdots &amp;\\ddots &amp;\\vdots\\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0&amp; 0&amp; 0&amp; 0&amp; \\cdots &amp; -n+2 \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix}c_0 \\\\c_1 \\\\c_2\\\\c_3\\\\c_4\\\\c_5\\\\ \\vdots \\\\ c_n \\end{bmatrix} =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\0 \\\\0\\\\0\\\\0\\\\0\\\\ \\vdots \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -83px\" width=\"448\" height=\"175\" />\n</p><p>This matrix is singular because the 3nd row and the 4rd row also start at the 3rd column, then all coefficients <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e95be43c04d6869c67861aae1e3e69123fedd8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/2517ce15b7189285d40592f59ae313e758b1f42e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> need to be zero so that the coefficient in front of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is zero.\n</p><p>That is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f980a64290e90d04964927ca1b8230300bc7496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_3=c_4=c_5=\\cdots =c_n=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>So now we just need to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/00322295674c54c5413520f7493470ff32ae3cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d4142d351ef99cc26a94e44c1912d904dd4a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, for that we look at the coefficient in front of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de8fdaa56ea5a8940d4bba79faa9e3dea0f6bf7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1d6febede10aaac4a13a74b969c2ab9d4c942fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( c_1-c_0+\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(-1)^{i-1}\\binom{i}{i-1}c_i+\\sum_{i=0}^{n}(-1)^{i}\\binom{i}{i}c_i \\right)x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"422\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e95be43c04d6869c67861aae1e3e69123fedd8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />=0 for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/2517ce15b7189285d40592f59ae313e758b1f42e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/c/7ac8eb48a78a4ac199f8b42761e52721218390c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( c_1-c_0+\\sum_{i=1}^{2}(-1)^{i-1}\\binom{i}{i-1}c_i+\\sum_{i=0}^{2}(-1)^{i}\\binom{i}{i}c_i \\right)x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"422\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/7/077959af9c1dceec3b28342bea2f340c5c61f120.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( c_1-c_0+\\binom{1}{0}c_1-\\binom{2}{1}c_2+c_0-c_1+c_2\\right)x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"358\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec5306284cd3a9a38627ac3016afc958bdcc14b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( c_1-c_0+c_1-2c_2+c_0-c_1+c_2\\right)x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"279\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/f/7ef912be997495c538c00e5ef30891a94b1ed258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(c_1-c_2\\right)x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d035e2c1de83d2dae3fb4ae591ee94ef8b2bbe96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1-c_2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/7/7b757bd66e34f08729982e114dd4fb69e706b9f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1=c_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> satisfies the condition for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de8fdaa56ea5a8940d4bba79faa9e3dea0f6bf7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> to be a constant polynomial.\n</p><p>So we can set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/e/54e6e0a09eb63b43fb69033f0f474a39f0e7333d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1=c_2=A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/1/fe1a2242bc6435b7fb163f30fff7db23ea075b43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_0=B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"17\" />, and all the polynomials <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> will be in the form:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c83ba50d3ca7e06929b4ada9bfacd57776ea872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)=Ax^2+Ax+B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"21\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/f/9ef636621ab05daa484a93cc57dd47d78dccc98c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B \\in \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>~Tomas Diaz. orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017232632\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.041 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 179/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 368/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11667/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    9.636      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    9.636      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25913:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017232632 and revision id 206089. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}